# Normalize line endings; scripts must be LF.
# POSIX sh chokes on CRLF shebangs (`#!/bin/sh\r`) even though
# Git-for-Windows tolerates them — pin every executable script to LF.
* text=auto
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
# The comment above says "pin every executable script to LF" but `*.mjs` was not
# pinned, so the repo's own statement was only half true (review P3-21). `* text=auto`
# does normalize it, but it normalizes to the *platform* default: a Windows clone
# gets CRLF and a POSIX sh run of a .mjs gets the same broken shebang the rule
# exists to prevent. Pinned explicitly rather than left to the blanket rule.
*.mjs text eol=lf
# Biome's formatter requires LF; a CRLF checkout of a JSON config fails
# the gate (plan §7). Pin the configs it checks so fresh clones stay LF.
*.json text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
# Same reason: biome formats CSS and rejects a CRLF stylesheet.
*.css text eol=lf
# rustfmt: keep Rust sources LF so a checkout on any OS formats identically.
*.rs text eol=lf
